WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.997
For the third guided practice the business question
is list all patients

00:00:04.024 --> 00:00:09.277
and show glucose tests when they exist The words all
patients are

00:00:09.291 --> 00:00:16.063
the key They tell us the patient population must
remain complete Run

00:00:16.089 --> 00:00:20.816
the query with the glucose condition inside ON
Confirm that all patients

00:00:20.842 --> 00:00:25.869
are present and that only glucose lab rows can match
Then think

00:00:25.882 --> 00:00:30.753
back to the WHERE-trap example Moving the same
test-name condition into WHERE

00:00:30.766 --> 00:00:34.872
removes patients whose lab columns are NULL so the
population becomes only

00:00:34.885 --> 00:00:40.456
patients with glucose tests Try to explain the
difference without using the

00:00:40.482 --> 00:00:45.235
words because SQL does it that way Instead use the
concepts of

00:00:45.248 --> 00:00:51.515
matching and final filtering ON limits eligible
matches WHERE

00:00:51.541 --> 00:00:56.159
filters the joined rows after preservation has
already created NULL-extended rows
